# detail
Number of changes: 1

1. Modified | Loop code block
   Replaced the original loop implementation that iterated according to the number of nodes and called `process_edge` for each edge to test feasibility with a loop that iterates according to `numb_nodes` and updates distances and predecessors based on `dist`.
   The original implementation included:

   * Loop statement: iterate over `range(G.number_of_nodes())`;
   * Assignment statement: set `feasible = True`;
   * Loop statement: iterate over `G.edges()`;
   * Conditional statement: obtain the edge weight `edata` according to `G.is_multigraph()`;
   * Conditional statement: call `process_edge(u, v, edata)` and update `feasible`;
   * Conditional statement: for an undirected graph, when the reverse edge did not exist, call `process_edge(v, u, edata)` and update `feasible`;
   * Conditional statement: execute `break` when `feasible` was true.

   The new implementation includes:

   * Loop statement: iterate over `range(numb_nodes)`;
   * Assignment statement: set `no_changes = True`;
   * Loop statement: iterate over `list(dist.items())`;
   * Loop statement: iterate over `G[u].items()`;
   * Assignment statement: compute `dist_v = dist_u + get_weight(edict)`;
   * Conditional statement: when `v` was not in `dist` or `dist[v] > dist_v`, update `dist[v]`, `pred[v]`, and `no_changes`;
   * Conditional statement: execute `break` when `no_changes` was true.
# /detail
# mode：Modify for loop (change iterable and loop logic)
